{"aggregate_id": "01M57FKP4Z0HV4E5AQVPQEKX31", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01M57FKS36E4Q5MV80YBSZZF7H", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"actor": "stijn@spec-kitty.ai", "created_at": "2026-10-18T12:25:59.306008+00:00", "friendly_name": "Fix plan-mission guard/manifest artifact-vocabulary mismatch", "mission_id": "01M57FKP4Z0HV4E5AQVPQEKX31", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "plan-guard-artifact-vocabulary-01M57FKP", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "On main (4.0.0rc8) a built-in plan mission is hard-blocked at specify: next reports 'Required artifact missing: spec.md' even with spec.md committed, and guard_failure_paths is empty (#6388, P0). The plan guard chain checks spec.md/research.md/plan.md (what the step contracts actually produce) but the plan expected-artifacts.yaml manifest declares goals.md under phase step-keys goals/draft, so the presence gatherer never looks for spec.md and required_artifacts_for returns nothing. This mission reconciles the manifest (and the descriptive mission.yaml copies) to the runtime action vocabulary, restores guard_failure_paths, and adds the parity + completeness guards that would have caught the drift.", "purpose_tldr": "Let a built-in plan mission advance past specify by reconciling the plan family's expected-artifacts manifest with the artifacts its step contracts and guards actually use.", "target_branch": "fix/plan-guard-artifact-vocabulary", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "spec-kitty", "project_uuid": "8a4a7da6-a97c-4bb4-893a-b31664abfee4", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-10-18T12:26:02.214625+00:00"}
